 "note": "TEST_EXISTING v6 target (public-test-case-existing-v6): 14 exported functions from 13 permissive repos outside lm-corpus (repo and module sha checked against ext-manifest 8458eac6 + ext-corpus.json), each called by an existing test file at the pinned commit (HEAD of the clone), where v1-v5 refuse the function (test_target_signature) and v6 accepts it on the pinned module text, following relative imports only through the pinned sibling fixtures (0 examples need a sibling). The examples cover both v6 widenings: 8 take a parameter typed exactly `unknown`, and 6 take a `NodeJS.ProcessEnv` parameter (4 of them with the default `= process.env`, which v6 allows only when every check passes the env object). Method: the HEAD scan of the same 411 + 326 cloned permissive TypeScript repos used for M88-M91 found 123 candidates (at most 3 per repo; 3 in Peace's repos); 107 replay and pass the license and size (64 KiB) checks, 93 of those pass the pre-push core-text scan. Kept: every NodeJS.ProcessEnv example (11, 10 repos) plus the 8 smallest `unknown` examples from other repos (one per repo; a fork carrying a byte-identical module was skipped). Auditor #460 (2nd review) rebuild: replayed on the full clone with the closure rules (load-time reach, non-.ts relative imports, require / dynamic import in the closure); 4 ProcessEnv examples are now correctly refused there (casper terminalPrompt, vskill resolveGitHubEnvToken, aidlc-workflows inNightly, scriptc resolvePlatformLinker: test_target_io) and openswarm resolveEscalationBudget was dropped because its newly needed closure fixtures fail the pre-push core-text scan, leaving 6 ProcessEnv examples. Peace's public repos were checked first (see peace): PeaceSTOCKS has fitting functions, but it is in the corpus manifest, so they are recorded and not counted.",
